      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A thangka, variously spelt as thangka, tangka, thanka, or tanka is a Tibetan
    Buddhist painting on cotton, silk appliqu\xE9, usually depicting a Buddhist deity,
    scene, or mandala. Thangkas are traditionally kept unframed and rolled up when
    not on display, mounted on a textile backing somewhat in the style of Chinese
    scroll paintings, with a further silk cover on the front. So treated, thangkas
    can last a long time, but because of their delicate nature, they have to be kept
    in dry places where moisture will not affect the quality of the silk."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 37a1986b4660442c295a534dc348a9c8, type: 2}
